# avia.js

What it is: Aviation tab: the numbers that do not come from the flight records
File: src/data/presets/avia.js
SHA-256: 46c71af389410fc4ee2e0857a6651fe39f7b1d9d4ea30fd0fe8160effcb0bc1f
Obtained: typed by hand (or OCR checked by hand) from a printed or scanned source.
Made by: by hand
From: The cruise speed chosen for the level-flight figures (250 m/s at 10,668 m); the two aircraft
  of the force figure; three airports for the heading indicators; EI-GJT (Boeing 737-800, 9 October
  2018): its inertial ground speed read by eye off figure 3 of AAIB Bulletin 12/2019 (a PDF), and
  its track off figure 4; One More Orbit (Gulfstream G650ER, 9-11 July 2019): times from the FAI
  record and the mission's site; the airports' short names are ours.
Licence: other: facts with their sources (each in the file)
What could still be wrong: The EI-GJT speeds are read off a printed figure, about ±2 % on each
  point; the start and heading of its track are decoration, not data.
